#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:5
#: fc5e73a8a9494d0796d6a529da090de7
msgid "Drift Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:7
#: 0252dd145f6c49d0969583b04527edef
msgid "This page provides tips for flying in Drift Mode and methods for tuning your copter to fly optimally in Drift Mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:11
#: 6d546c3ca3fd4a3687c62c66a59a6b3e
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:13
#: 032a9f202cff48a6ab64f78de68ede59
msgid "Drift Mode allows the user to fly a multi-copter as if it were a plane with built in automatic coordinated turns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:15
#: 5ede97fa742f49e7ba8431f736e48e47
msgid "The user has direct control of Yaw and Pitch, but Roll is controlled by the autopilot.  This allows the copter to be controlled very intuitively with a single control stick if using a Mode 2 transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:18
#: ca8af1867a60439cb295774648bf0765
msgid "The user has completely manual control over the throttle as in :ref:`Stabilize mode <stabilize-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:25
#: e771317411b94d27a5b21d9e2332f966
msgid "How Drift Mode works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:27
#: ca03ada09b8145adaccc540101b2fe46
msgid "You \"fly\" the MultiCopter with the right stick (on Mode 2 controllers) controls Pitch and Yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:29
#: 184e91030c7149bc8444ea944608ee0d
msgid "You use the left stick primarily for altitude control but not for yaw directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:31
#: 1680d291e07b48748d6dbc7c9fdc272a
msgid "When you push the right stick forward or back the copter will pitch (and accelerate) in the appropriate direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:33
#: 46b7e0ac853b4652b327bf5c58c1a84f
msgid "When you push the right stick towards one side or the other the right or to the left the copter will turn in the direction specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:35
#: f0aa98804fe0454bb5ca7fd5d539b155
msgid "The copter will also bank at the same time so as to make a coordinated turn in that direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:37
#: 946d14f0d5674650a588957ba3287351
msgid "When turning with the right stick yaw is automatically applied and sufficient roll is added to cancel the copters velocity in the roll axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:40
#: 586df2ebbf7d42b988ac50204c887bbf
msgid "This allows you to maintain a coordinated (non-skidding) turn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:41
#: b493144ebbaa411faacd96242929a397
msgid "Letting go of the sticks effectively turns on a speed brake in the Pitch axis that slows the copter to a stop over a two second period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:43
#: f8e82338b9f4460bad5c1e11ff54817c
msgid "A copter in Drift Mode with the right stick in the center will loosely hold horizontal position (It will slowly drift in the wind.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:45
#: c3ff5a42cc414cbfbc0c9e4f7b85e4a3
msgid "Pilot’s throttle input controls the average motor speed meaning that constant adjustment of the throttle is required to maintain altitude.  If the pilot puts the throttle completely down the motors will go to their minimum rate (:ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>`) and if the vehicle is flying it will lose attitude control and tumble."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:50
#: 17c8608736f441b09d965638c2277137
msgid "Drift Mode relies on a valid position estimate, such as GPS, for control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:51
#: e60a769e1cb1400eba8eb8d1bb006f35
msgid "If you lose your GPS signal in flight while in Drift Mode, your copter will either land or enter altitude hold based on your :ref:`FS_EKF_ACTION <FS_EKF_ACTION>` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:54
#: cc86c88e43b4445c8b386e7c3061672c
msgid "You should also be prepared to switch back to Stabilize Mode for manual recovery if necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:58
#: ea86f3ac6f824b149f8672bfdea5a3ad
msgid "What's it Useful For"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:60
#: bde5096383a644ce975d56766f65bbbb
msgid "FPV flyers who are looking for a dynamic, plane like flight as well as loiter-like position hold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:62
#: d4d3cea2db194ff1859a5580b72e1711
msgid "New flyers who want to try a more intuitive and easy to learn flight mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:64
#: e7aa946373c1477584da1fae3eee04ca
msgid "Anybody who would like to try an easy to fly and easy to learn and very fun mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:66
#: a2a4a9149a04452ca8dc488138f7e858
msgid "Photographers and especially videographers who want a smoother and more coordinated filming result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:70
#: b5ae47d23a6f4fe4ac179ab2006da864
msgid "Setting up Drift Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:72
#: 68184cdc4c534338b53ae19ae645acbe
msgid "In the Mission Planner Configuration Section under flight modes select Drift Mode to apply to an appropriate switch setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drift-mode.rst:74
#: bd5de557f2a04aa3982f357d3da26e86
msgid "More information on tuning Drift mode is expected to be forthcoming shortly as are additional enhancements to Drift Mode itself."
msgstr ""
